# Line endings are normalized so a Windows checkout and the Linux CI runner
# always agree. Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked
# out with LF, so editing on Windows never produces a whole-file CRLF diff.
# Measured 2026-10-17: all 245 text files in the index were already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF: CRLF breaks the shebang on Linux runners.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets are never touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
